{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>HaElohim has found.</b> We know that we have done no wrong, but from the Omnipresent it came to bring this upon us — a creditor finds an opportunity to collect his bond." "<b>How shall we justify ourselves.</b> From the root צֶדֶק. And so every word whose root begins with צַדִ\"י and comes in the hitpa'el or nif'al pattern — a טֵי\"ת replaces the תָי\"ו, and it is not placed before the first letter of the root but in the middle of the root letters, e.g. נִצְטַדַּק from the root צדק; וְיִצְטַבַּע from the root צבע; וַיִּצְטַיָּרוּ from the root וְצִיר אֱמוּנִים; הִצְטַיַּדְנוּ from the root צֵדָה לַדֶּרֶךְ. And a word whose root begins with סָמֶ\"ךְ or שִׁי\"ן — when it is in the hitpa'el, the תָי\"ו separates the root letters, e.g. וְיִסְתַּבֵּל הֶחָגָב (Ecclesiastes 12), from the root סבל; מִשְׁתַּכַּל הֲוֵית בְּקַרְנַיָּא (Daniel 7); וְיִשְׁתַּמֵּר חֻקּוֹת עָמְרִי (Micah 6), from the root שמר; וְסָר מֵרָע מִשְׁתּוֹלֵל (Isaiah 59), from the root מוֹלִיךְ יוֹעֲצִים שׁוֹלָל (Job 12); מִסְתּוֹלֵל בְּעַמִּי (Exodus 15), from the root דֶּרֶךְ לֹא סְלוּלָה (Jeremiah 18)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:34.171446390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}